
== P  primitives
CONFIRMED P1: pauliW (cnot w) = U pauliW(w) U^dagger with U = CNOT (control first qubit), symbolic w: cnot is the CNOT conjugation, so cnot Q3 = Q3 and cnot is an ipW-isometric involution
CONFIRMED P2: cnot (cnot w) = w and ipW (cnot E) (cnot w) = ipW E w, symbolic (hence ipW E (cnot w) = ipW (cnot E) w)
CONFIRMED P3: trace pairing: tr(opW E . pauliW w) = ipW E w, symbolic; with pauliW onto Hermitian matrices, Q3 <-> PSD and dualW Q3 = {E : opW E PSD} (PSD self-duality, written)
CONFIRMED P4: actT reflY = partial transpose on token 2, actC reflY = on token 1, both = full transpose; PT1 = (PT2)^T; actT reflY is an ipW-self-adjoint involution. Hence actC reflY Q3 = actT reflY Q3 = twin, D Q3 D = Q3, and dualW twin = actT reflY (dualW Q3) (written from these identities)

== M  the mixed assignment (Q3, Q3, Q3, twin)
CONFIRMED M1: phiW in Q3; phiW/4 in dualW Q3; sing4 in Q3; L' = actT reflY sing4 = [1, -1, 1, -1] in twin; L'/4 in dualW twin
CONFIRMED M1e: complements E00 - phiW/4 and E00 - sing4/4 lie in dualW Q3: the dual tables are effects (values in [0, 1])
CONFIRMED M2: famI(X = phiW in K01, Y = phiW in K23, E = phiW/4 in dualW K02, F = L'/4 in dualW K13 = dualW twin) = -1/8
CONFIRMED M3: famII(L = phiW in K02, L' in K13 = twin, e = phiW/4, f = phiW/4 in dualW Q3) = -1/8
CONFIRMED M2c: countercontrols with the twin argument replaced by a Q3 one: famI 1/4, famII 1/4

== T  per-token transport and the 16 twist patterns of {Q3, twin}^4 (pairs 01, 23, 02, 13)
CONFIRMED T1: for all 16 token charts g, famI and famII are unchanged when the table of each pair (i, j) is replaced by D^g_i . T . D^g_j (symbolic, 64 variables)
CONFIRMED T1c: countercontrol: reflecting token 0 in X alone changes famI
CONFIRMED T2: the coboundaries of the 4-cycle are exactly the 8 even patterns
CONFIRMED T3: each of the 8 odd patterns: the transported witnesses are members of that pattern's cones and duals (checked directly), with (famI, famII) values [(-1/8, -1/8)]
  NOTE [written] even patterns: by T1 FCC(tau) <=> FCC(0) for every coboundary tau, and FCC(0) (uniform Q3) holds by the trace pairing P3 with the Kronecker product of PSD matrices (landed probe F2/F3, replayed byte-identically). So on {Q3, twin}^4, FCC holds exactly at the 8 even patterns (thread C B2 confirmed).

== K  the uniform foil K_c = cone(SEP u cnot SEP)
CONFIRMED K1: hom x^T E0 hom y = x1*y3 - x2*y2 + 1; Lagrange identity (x1^2+x2^2)(y3^2+y2^2) - (x1 y3 - x2 y2)^2 = (x1 y2 + x2 y3)^2; cnot E0 = E0. Hence |x1 y3 - x2 y2| <= |x||y| <= 1 on the ball, E0 >= 0 on SEP, and by P2 on cnot SEP: E0 in dualW K_c
CONFIRMED K2: E0 is not in dualW Q3 (opW E0 has a negative eigenvalue): K_c is a proper subcone of Q3
CONFIRMED K3: pauliW (prodState x y) = rho_x (x) rho_y, symbolic (products PSD on the ball); with P1, K_c is inside Q3. G is in Q3 = dualW Q3 (as sets), hence G in dualW K_c
CONFIRMED K4: phiW = cnot (prodState xplus z3): phiW lies in cnot SEP, so in K_c
CONFIRMED K5: famI(phiW, phiW, E0, G) = -1: famI fails for uniform K_c and for (Q3, Q3, K_c, K_c); famII(L = phiW, L' = phiW, e = E0, f = G) = -1: famII fails for (K_c, K_c, Q3, Q3)
CONFIRMED K5c: countercontrol: with the unit E00 in place of E0 the value is 1 > 0
CONFIRMED K6: R is a rotation; actC R phiW = G; ipW E0 G = -1 with E0 in dualW K_c: G is not in K_c, so actC R does not map K_c into itself and IE1 (K_c) fails (IE1 asks actC R K = K for every rotation)
CONFIRMED K6c: countercontrol: the same rotation keeps phiW inside Q3 (IE1 of Q3 is not refuted)
  NOTE [written] uniform K_c with cnot gates and identity locals: hcls holds (NClass with identity locals is N = cnot); hadm: products in K_c by definition, K_c inside Q3 inside maxCone (P3 with the Lorentz-cone factorization), convex cone; hcl: generated by a compact base avoiding 0; hgate: cnot exchanges SEP and cnot SEP (P2). So the four pair hypotheses hold and FCC and C fail (K5, K6): thread C B4 confirmed.

== A  the A2 route: linear algebra of step 3
CONFIRMED A1: the 16 token products tp s t (s, t in S = {e_x, e_y, e_z, -e_z}) have det 256 and flat index 0 equal to 1: a basis of R^16 inside H00
CONFIRMED A2: a general bi-affine map (289 coefficients) restricted to H00 x H00 equals the bilinear form u^T C' w with C' = M + beta e0^T + e0 gamma^T + alpha e0 e0^T: two bi-affine maps that agree on basis x basis inside H00 agree on H00 x H00 (with A1)
CONFIRMED A3: Psi(tp x0 x2, tp x1 x3)_abcd = tabCoord a b (tp x0 x1) * tabCoord c d (tp x2 x3) for all a, b, c, d, symbolic x: under N2 and prodEff_apply the two bi-affine maps of step 3 agree at the 256 points

== S  the MSIG carrier (thread C A3, converse direction)
CONFIRMED S1: sigma is an involution of R^{17x17} (289 basis arrays) and sigma iota = iota R (symbolic)
CONFIRMED S2: N2 in MSIG for all token vectors (symbolic x0..x3 in R^3): PB.prodState (tp x0 x2) (tp x1 x3) = sigma (pState ..) = pState (tp x0 x1) (tp x2 x3) = PA.prodState ..; and PB.prodEff e f := pEff e f o sigma satisfies the evaluation law by S1
CONFIRMED S3: cross values: for normalized X, Y (entry (0,0) = 1) and general affine e, f, PB.prodEff e f (PA.prodState X Y) = famI(X, Y, E~, F~) and, read the other way, PA.prodEff e f (PB.prodState L L') = famII(L, L', e~, f~), with E~ the homogenized coefficient table (symbolic)
CONFIRMED S4: the unit pairing is 1 at the other grouping's normalized products (prodEff_unit on the hull body)
  NOTE [written] with hadm (K inside maxCone, so a maxCone table with entry (0,0) = 0 vanishes), an effect e on pairBody K has E~ in dualW K; FCC gives each cross value >= 0, and with the complement E00 - E~ and famI(X, Y, E00, E00) = 1, each is <= 1. By S2-S4 MSIG with Omega = conv(A products u B products) satisfies N0, N1, N2: FCC and hadm imply the existence of a carrier with N0 and N1 and N2 (thread C A3 confirmed).

== B  scope of the tree obstruction (thread C B3)
CONFIRMED B1: gate maps: D^a cnot(D^a w D^b) D^b is cnot for a = b and cnotTw = actT reflY . cnot . actT reflY for a != b (symbolic): per-token charts carry cones and gate maps of the quantum data onto those of M_tok on every 3-pair subset (with T2 and R1 of thread C)
CONFIRMED B2: M_tok's twist pattern is a coboundary on every 3-pair subset, not on the cycle
CONFIRMED B3: each Pi_S ("the post-local determinant pattern on the 3-pair subset S is a chart image of the quantum one") is chart-invariant (enumeration, 256 patterns x 16 charts) and holds at the quantum data; at M_tok's locals it fails on [['01', '23', '13'], ['23', '02', '13']]: there the chart does not carry the quantum locals onto M_tok's
CONFIRMED B4: Pi_{01,23,02} and Pi_{01,23,13} together imply EvenCycle of the orientation bits (enumeration over all 256 patterns), and fail at all 16 patterns with M_tok's orientation bits (0,0,0,1), i.e. at every NClass decomposition of M_tok's gates (orientation is a gate invariant, thread D T2)
CONFIRMED B5: twin is not inside Q3 (actT reflY phiW = idW, pauliW idW not PSD) and cnotTw maps the product state (xplus, z3) to idW, so cnot does not map twin into twin
  NOTE [written] B5 with P1 and P4: an NClass gate L . cnot . L' (L = actC A . actT B) preserves Q3 only if det A det B = det A' det B' = 1, and preserves twin only if det A det B = -1. So on cones in {Q3, twin} with hcls and hgate the orientation bits equal the twist bits; with B4, the conjunction of "each cone is Q3 or twin" (one pair each) and the two 3-pair conditions of B4, all chart-invariant, implies an even twist pattern and hence FCC (T1-T3). So B3 holds for conditions on cones and gate MAPS (or reading the locals only through the gate), as in thread C's B5 wording "intrinsic condition on at most three pair cones"; it fails for conditions that may read the supplied locals, as the B3 header states.

AUDIT-C ALL CONFIRMED
